#38427
The Center of the Jousting Field~
   The jousting field is a long strip of earth about 200 feet in length.  Each
Knight on their steed proceeds to either end of the field and awaits signal.  
Once given, the knights charge forward and meet their lances at this point, the
goal being to knock the opposing knight off their steed.  Once dismounted, both
knights may draw their swords and fight blade to blade.  Given that either of
them are able to stand.    
~
